300	     * the current server date — exceeds one year (strictly more than one elapsed fiscal year). The
301	     * elapsed count is the difference between the fiscal year of the current server date and the
302	     * fiscal year of the registration date. This gates the top membership level: only an owner past
303	     * a full year of tenure can reach level 4. A {@code null} registration date counts as zero
304	     * tenure and so never exceeds the threshold, which is why a newly created owner (zero tenure)
305	     * can never exceed level 3.
